From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lo=C3=AFc=20Vigneron?= <loic.vigneron@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:23:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] staging: media: tegra-video: Allow cache hints

Buffers are allocated coherent, which on Tegra210 maps them uncached
for the CPU: reading a 1536x864 10-bit frame then took about 20 ms.
With cache hints allowed, user space can request
V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT buffers, which vb2 maps cached and
syncs for the CPU at dequeue; the same read takes about 7 ms.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/vi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/vi.c b/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/vi.c
index 8824951..fd9bc7c 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/vi.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/tegra-video/vi.c
@@ -1192,6 +1192,7 @@ static int tegra_channel_init(struct tegra_vi_channel *chan)
 	chan->queue.mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
 	chan->queue.timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_MONOTONIC;
 	chan->queue.min_queued_buffers = 2;
+	chan->queue.allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	chan->queue.dev = vi->dev;
 	ret = vb2_queue_init(&chan->queue);
 	if (ret < 0) {
